continuous increase during the subsequent thermal annealing for the target case, which is in contrast to the observation of the control case and led to a significant difference in the PL intensity between the two films. This indicates that with the EMIMHSO4 addition, the stacking defects of $a-F A P b|_{3}$ are continuously eliminated during thermal annealing. This reduction process can possibly be realized by defect passivation by $E M I M H S O_{4}.$ , for instance, through the interaction between ${\mathsf{H S O}}_{4}^{-}$ and undercoordinated $\mathsf{P b}^{2+}$ . Therefore, the decrease in stacking defects results in the suppression of nonradiative recombination. The PL peak and FWHM values remained unchanged after recrystallization irrespective of the $E M I M H S O_{4}$ addition (Figure 2e), suggesting the completion of the growth of α- $\mathsf{F A P b l}_{3}$ crystals. These observations indicate that the stacking defects of $a-F A P b|_{3}$ during thermal annealing, which are inevitably generated during $8–F A P b\mathsf{l}_{3}-\mathsf{a}$ -FAPbI3 conversion, can be efficiently and in situ eliminated during the conversion of precursors – solvates – $\mathfrak{a}$ -FAPbI3.
Based on the observations of different conversion pathways and stacking faults revealed by in-situ GIWAXS, UV–Vis, and PL spectroscopies, we propose the underlying mechanism in Figure 3. Generally, the conversion pathway of precursors – $-\delta\mathrm{-}\mathsf{F A P b l_{3}}-\mathsf{a-F A P b l_{3}}$ is highly tended because of the low formation energy of -FAPbI3.[20, 40] However, stacking defects were formed during the conversion of - $\mathsf{F A P b l_{3}}-\mathsf{a}\mathsf{-F A P b l_{3}}$ . The addition of EMIMHSO4 changes the thermal dynamics of the conversion pathway from precursors – $-\delta\mathrm{-}\mathsf{F A P b l_{3}}-\mathsf{a}\mathrm{-}\mathsf{F A P b l_{3}}$ to precursors – solvates – $\mathsf{a-F A P b l}_{3}$ , which is ascribed to the lower barrier energy of the precursors – solvates conversion pathway in the presence of precursors – EMIMHSO4 interaction. Compared to the fast conversion dynamics of $8–F A P b l_{3}-a-F A P b l_{3}$ during thermal annealing, the conversion of solvates – $-a-F A P b|_{3}$ requires a longer window to complete the solvents – FA exchange. In fact, the changed conversion pathways and prolonged conversion dynamics play a key role in the stacking of $\mathsf{a-F A P b l}_{3}$ . The stacking defects for $a-F A P b|_{3}$ crystals continuously decreased in situ with the $E M I M H S O_{4}$ addition. Overall, these multimodal in situ observations demonstrate the key role of how polytypes convert to $a-F A P b\mid_{3}$ in the formation and regulation of stacking defects during conversion.
